/* The SDK's own line (pico_standard_link/script_include), then the Intel
   decimal library's tables: its source declares them without const, so
   they'd be .data -- 33 KB copied into RAM at boot -- though nothing ever
   writes them (its only variables, the rounding mode and the flags, are
   .bss). Placed here, in .rodata, they stay in flash and the heap gets
   the 33 KB. .rodata comes before .data in the script, so these rules
   take the sections first. */
*(EXCLUDE_FILE(*libgcc.a: *libc.a: *lib*_a-mem*.o *libm.a:) .rodata*)
*libbid.a:*(.data .data.*)
